      <div id="childContent">
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681115"
      id="7681115"
      data-guid="7681115"
      data-position="3030"
      data-full-title="§ 133-3: Construction and alteration."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681115_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681115_label" for="7681115_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681115"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-3
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681115"
    >
Construction and alteration.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681115" data-guid="7681115"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681115" data-guid="7681115" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681115_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">No structure or part thereof shall hereafter be built or altered in the City of Albany except in conformity with the provisions of this code.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681116"
      id="7681116"
      data-guid="7681116"
      data-position="3031"
      data-full-title="§ 133-4: Filing of plans, specifications and statements."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681116_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681116_label" for="7681116_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681116"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-4
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681116"
    >
Filing of plans, specifications and statements.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681116" data-guid="7681116"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681116" data-guid="7681116" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681116_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">Before the erection or alteration of any structure is commenced, the owner or lessee, agent, architect or builder employed in connection with the proposed erection or alteration shall submit to the Superintendent of Buildings plans and specifications of the contemplated structure or alteration thereof.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681117"
      id="7681117"
      data-guid="7681117"
      data-position="3032"
      data-full-title="§ 133-5: Submittal of plans; contents."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681117_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681117_label" for="7681117_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681117"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-5
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681117"
    >
Submittal of plans; contents.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681117" data-guid="7681117"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681117" data-guid="7681117" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681117_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">A complete copy of the plans of the proposed work shall be submitted in duplicate to the Department of Buildings in blue or white prints or on paper in ink drawn to a scale. These plans shall indicate the street or lot number and shall include a plot plan showing the location of the structure in question in reference to the lot lines, which may, however, be indicated on the foundation or basement plan. These drawings shall include a foundation, cellar and basement plan and plans of every story, except where two or more stories shall be identical, a roof plan, longitudinal and transverse sections and all exposed elevations, also code of materials. Such plans shall be complete in detail as to the exact alteration, improvement or modification of the premises. Duplicate copies of the contract between the owner and contractor shall be submitted with the plans.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681118"
      id="7681118"
      data-guid="7681118"
      data-position="3033"
      data-full-title="§ 133-6: Steel or concrete construction; framing plans."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681118_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681118_label" for="7681118_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681118"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-6
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681118"
    >
Steel or concrete construction; framing plans.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681118" data-guid="7681118"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681118" data-guid="7681118" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681118_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">In cases where the construction of the building is of steel or reinforced concrete, framing plans shall be submitted. These plans shall be accompanied by such structural detail drawings as the Superintendent of Buildings may require.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681119"
      id="7681119"
      data-guid="7681119"
      data-position="3034"
      data-full-title="§ 133-7: Filing of plan copies."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681119_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681119_label" for="7681119_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681119"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-7
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681119"
    >
Filing of plan copies.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681119" data-guid="7681119"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681119" data-guid="7681119" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681119_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">One copy of the above plans shall, after being properly stamped, be returned to the applicant and the other kept on file in the office of the Superintendent of Buildings.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681120"
      id="7681120"
      data-guid="7681120"
      data-position="3035"
      data-full-title="§ 133-8: Specifications."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681120_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681120_label" for="7681120_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681120"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-8
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681120"
    >
Specifications.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681120" data-guid="7681120"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681120" data-guid="7681120" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681120_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">For all buildings within the fire limits and for all buildings other than frame buildings outside of the fire limits, typewritten copies in duplicate of the complete specifications shall be submitted to the Superintendent of Buildings, who, when he shall have approved the same and certified thereto, shall retain one copy and return the other to the applicant.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681121"
      id="7681121"
      data-guid="7681121"
      data-position="3036"
      data-full-title="§ 133-9: Statements."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681121_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681121_label" for="7681121_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681121"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-9
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681121"
    >
Statements.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681121" data-guid="7681121"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681121" data-guid="7681121" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681121_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">For all frame buildings outside of the fire limits there may be substituted for the specifications a detailed statement in triplicate on blanks furnished by the Superintendent of Buildings.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681122"
      id="7681122"
      data-guid="7681122"
      data-position="3037"
      data-full-title="§ 133-10: Required information; liability policy. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681122_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681122_label" for="7681122_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681122"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-10
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681122"
    >
Required information; liability policy.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681122" data-guid="7681122"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681122" data-guid="7681122" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681122_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">8-16-1993</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The plans and specifications or statements shall be accompanied with the full name and address of the owner or owners of the structure. For the purpose of this code, any person, firm or corporation holding the fee title to real property, or his or their duly authorized agent or attorney or the guardian, conservator or trustee, shall be regarded as the owner. The owner or contractor shall be required to have a liability policy in the amount of one hundred thousand/three hundred thousand dollars ($100,000/$300,000.) for personal injury and $50,000 for property damage which will name the City as an insured or co-insured during the period of time the permit is in use, or until the permit expires or is revoked by the Commissioner of Buildings. Said liability policy naming the City of Albany an insured or co-insured shall not be required where work to be performed is estimated to be $10,000 or less, except where the work to be performed involves dangerous or hazardous materials or potentially dangerous or hazardous conditions, so as to affect the public health, safety and welfare. The Building Commissioner shall promulgate an official Building Department policy detailing potentially dangerous or hazardous conditions and/or materials which will require insurance pursuant to this section.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681123"
      id="7681123"
      data-guid="7681123"
      data-position="3038"
      data-full-title="§ 133-11: Additional information. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681123_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681123_label" for="7681123_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681123"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-11
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681123"
    >
Additional information.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681123" data-guid="7681123"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681123" data-guid="7681123" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681123_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">2-19-1987</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681124"><a alt="133-11A" class="litem_number" href="7681124#7681124" onclick="return false;" title="133-11A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">If the construction is to be executed by any other person than the owner of the land in fee, the name of the person or persons or corporation intending to make such erection or alteration shall also be given, together with a statement of their authority from the owner for such work.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681125"><a alt="133-11B" class="litem_number" href="7681125#7681125" onclick="return false;" title="133-11B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Where the construction activity may involve an obstruction to vehicular or pedestrian traffic, a permit for said obstruction shall be applied for pursuant to this section.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681126"><a alt="133-11C" class="litem_number" href="7681126#7681126" onclick="return false;" title="133-11C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">A barricade permit allowing a temporary obstruction will be issued at the discretion of the Building Commissioner after he has determined that any contemplated construction or demolition activity will be conducted pursuant to the generally accepted standards of the New York Uniform Code.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681127"><a alt="133-11D" class="litem_number" href="7681127#7681127" onclick="return false;" title="133-11D">D. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">For the purposes of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681110" href="7681110#7681110">1</a>, obstructions shall include but are not limited to any automobile, truck, van, crane, backhoe, grader, paver, scaffold, dumpster or any other materials or equipment which, in the determination of the Building Commissioner, would hinder or obstruct the safe passage of vehicular or pedestrian traffic.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681128"><a alt="133-11E" class="litem_number" href="7681128#7681128" onclick="return false;" title="133-11E">E. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The Building Commissioner shall have the authority to issue rules and regulations necessary to carry out the purposes of this section.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681129"
      id="7681129"
      data-guid="7681129"
      data-position="3044"
      data-full-title="§ 133-12: Approval required; posting of permit."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681129_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681129_label" for="7681129_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681129"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-12
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681129"
    >
Approval required; posting of permit.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681129" data-guid="7681129"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681129" data-guid="7681129" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681129_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">Except as otherwise herein provided, the erection or alteration of a structure, including any new siding of whatsoever type or nature, shall not be commenced until complete plans, specifications or statements shall have been submitted to and approved by the Commissioner of Buildings, and a permit posted in a conspicuous place on the premises. It shall be unlawful for any person to remove, mutilate, destroy or conceal any notice issued and posted on any building by the Commissioner of Buildings pursuant to the provisions of this code.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681130"
      id="7681130"
      data-guid="7681130"
      data-position="3045"
      data-full-title="§ 133-13: Temporary permits and certificates. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681130_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681130_label" for="7681130_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681130"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-13
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681130"
    >
Temporary permits and certificates.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681130" data-guid="7681130"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681130" data-guid="7681130" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681130_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Added <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">4-20-1987</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681131"><a alt="133-13A" class="litem_number" href="7681131#7681131" onclick="return false;" title="133-13A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">No provision of § <a class="xref" guid="7681129" href="7681129#7681129">133-12</a> shall be construed as preventing the Commissioner of Buildings from granting a temporary permit for the erection or alteration of any part of a structure where plans, specifications or statements have been presented for that portion of the same before the entire plans, specifications or statements have been submitted.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681132"><a alt="133-13B" class="litem_number" href="7681132#7681132" onclick="return false;" title="133-13B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">No land shall be occupied or used and no building hereafter erected or altered shall be occupied or used, in whole or in part, for any purpose whatsoever until a certificate of occupancy shall have been issued by the Commissioner of Buildings stating that the premises or buildings comply with all the provisions of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681110" href="7681110#7681110">1</a>. No change or extension of use and no alteration shall be made in a nonconforming use or premises without a certificate of occupancy having first been issued by the Commissioner of Buildings that such change, extension or alteration is in conformity with the provisions of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681110" href="7681110#7681110">1</a>. Nothing contained herein, however, shall prevent the Commissioner from promulgating and implementing rules and regulations governing the issuance of temporary certificates and/or the posting of adequate bond or other security to insure the timely completion of necessary work.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681133"
      id="7681133"
      data-guid="7681133"
      data-position="3048"
      data-full-title="§ 133-14: Construction to conform to plans, specifications or statements."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681133_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681133_label" for="7681133_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681133"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-14
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681133"
    >
Construction to conform to plans, specifications or statements.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681133" data-guid="7681133"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681133" data-guid="7681133" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681133_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The erection or alteration of any structure shall proceed in accordance with the plans, specifications or statements on which the permit has been issued. Any structural changes must first be submitted for approval of the Superintendent of Buildings and must be clearly shown by drawings, specifications or statements covering the proposed departure from the original construction.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681134"
      id="7681134"
      data-guid="7681134"
      data-position="3049"
      data-full-title="§ 133-15: Approval or rejection of application."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681134_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681134_label" for="7681134_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681134"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-15
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681134"
    >
Approval or rejection of application.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681134" data-guid="7681134"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681134" data-guid="7681134" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681134_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">It shall be the duty of the Superintendent of Buildings to approve or reject, within a reasonable time, plans, specifications or statements filed with him pursuant to the provisions of this section. If upon examination he shall find that plans and specifications filed with the Bureau of Buildings for approval contemplate work not in accordance with the Building Code, the Superintendent of Buildings shall indicate such deviations in writing on a correction sheet and return the plans and specifications with the correction sheet to the applicant, and no permit shall be issued until such deviations have been corrected or approved.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681135"
      id="7681135"
      data-guid="7681135"
      data-position="3050"
      data-full-title="§ 133-16: Expiration of permit."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681135_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681135_label" for="7681135_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681135"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-16
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681135"
    >
Expiration of permit.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681135" data-guid="7681135"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681135" data-guid="7681135" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681135_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">12-17-2012</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 2-2012</span></span>]</div><div class="para">Any permit issued by the Commissioner of Buildings and Regulatory Compliance shall expire upon the one-year anniversary of said permit, unless the permit holder has requested, and has received, an extension from the Department of Buildings and Regulatory Compliance.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681136"
      id="7681136"
      data-guid="7681136"
      data-position="3051"
      data-full-title="§ 133-17: Minor repairs."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681136_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681136_label" for="7681136_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681136"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-17
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681136"
    >
Minor repairs.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681136" data-guid="7681136"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681136" data-guid="7681136" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681136_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">Repairs of structures which do not involve a change in construction may be made without notice to the Bureau of Buildings, but such repairs shall not be construed to permit the cutting away of any wall or portion thereof, or the removal or cutting of any beams, girders or supports, or the changing or removal of any staircase, or the alteration of any drainage system.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681137"
      id="7681137"
      data-guid="7681137"
      data-position="3052"
      data-full-title="§ 133-18: Application of code."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681137_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681137_label" for="7681137_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681137"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-18
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681137"
    >
Application of code.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681137" data-guid="7681137"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681137" data-guid="7681137" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681137_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The foregoing provisions and all the provisions of this code shall apply with equal force to all buildings erected or altered within the City, both municipal and private.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681138"
      id="7681138"
      data-guid="7681138"
      data-position="3053"
      data-full-title="§ 133-19: License and permit fees. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681138_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681138_label" for="7681138_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681138"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-19
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681138"
    >
License and permit fees.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681138" data-guid="7681138"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681138" data-guid="7681138" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681138_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">10-17-1983</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681139"><a alt="133-19A" class="litem_number" href="7681139#7681139" onclick="return false;" title="133-19A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Building permit fees. Upon the filing of an application for a building permit, the Commissioner of Buildings shall have the authority to set reasonable and necessary fees for the issuance of all permits and/or certificates issued by the Department of Buildings pursuant to the Building Code, Housing Ordinance, Zoning Ordinance<a class="footnoteref" href="#ft7681139-1" id="ref7681139-1">[1]</a> or any other ordinance of the City of Albany requiring the issuance of a permit by the Department of Buildings. The amount of such fees shall be fixed in an amount sufficient to defray actual operating expenses incurred by the Department in the issuance of said permits and the administration of the functions related thereto.</div><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7681139-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7681139-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor's Note: See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7682800" href="7682800#7682800">231</a>, Housing, and Ch. <a class="xref" guid="38067105" href="38067105#38067105">375</a>, Unified Sustainable Development.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681140"><a alt="133-19B" class="litem_number" href="7681140#7681140" onclick="return false;" title="133-19B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The Commissioner shall maintain a list of all fees charged for the issuance of any permits by his Department, and such list shall be posted in the Building Department and shall be available to the public upon request.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681145"
      id="7681145"
      data-guid="7681145"
      data-position="3056"
      data-full-title="§ 133-20: Demolition or boarding up of buildings."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681145_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681145_label" for="7681145_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681145"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-20
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681145"
    >
Demolition or boarding up of buildings.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681145" data-guid="7681145"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681145" data-guid="7681145" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681145_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">11-16-2009</span> by <span class="loclaw">Ord. No. 68.102.09</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="14105218"><a alt="133-20A" class="litem_number" href="14105218#14105218" onclick="return false;" title="133-20A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">A permit shall be obtained for the demolition or boarding up of a building or part thereof. No permit shall be issued unless the applicant executes and delivers to the Director of Buildings a bond executed by a solvent surety company authorized to transact business in the State of New York, in an amount to be fixed by the Director of Buildings, providing for the holding harmless of the City of Albany and all its officers and departments from all damages which they may sustain or be liable for by reason of the demolition or boarding up of the structures for which the permit is applied, and the applicant shall also furnish the Director of Buildings with satisfactory evidence that the applicant carries insurance in a proper amount covering property damage to adjoining property and public liability insurance for the protection of the public.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="14105219"><a alt="133-20B" class="litem_number" href="14105219#14105219" onclick="return false;" title="133-20B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Before any such permit is issued, the applicant is required by law to secure workers' compensation insurance and shall file with the Director of Buildings proper evidence that such insurance has been secured.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="14105220"><a alt="133-20C" class="litem_number" href="14105220#14105220" onclick="return false;" title="133-20C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The permit when issued shall provide that the applicant will comply with all the laws of the State of New York and with the laws and ordinances of the City of Albany, and for failure so to do, the Director of Buildings may revoke such permit. Said permit may also be revoked without notice if in the opinion of the Director of Buildings or the Commissioner of the Department of General Services the demolition or boarding up of the building is being conducted in a dangerous or unsafe manner.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="14105221"><a alt="133-20D" class="litem_number" href="14105221#14105221" onclick="return false;" title="133-20D">D. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Notwithstanding the foregoing provisions of this section, no application for demolition under this section shall be approved without prior review and approval of the Planning Board established in accordance with Chapters <a class="xref" guid="7678876" href="7678876#7678876">42</a> and <a class="xref" guid="38067105" href="38067105#38067105">375</a> of the Code of the City of Albany.<a class="footnoteref" href="#ft14105221-1" id="ref14105221-1">[1]</a></div><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft14105221-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref14105221-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor’s Note: Former Subsection E, Submittal requirements for demolition application; planning standards and criteria, former Subsection F, which set forth considerations for the Planning Board with regard to demolitions, and former Subsection G, which required that a copy of a demolition application be submitted to the Director of Buildings, all of which immediately followed, were repealed 5-15-2017 by Ord. No. 26.31.17.</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 14105240"
      id="14105240"
      data-guid="14105240"
      data-position="3061"
      data-full-title="§ 133-21: Demolition for erection of new structure or new use."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="14105240_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="14105240_label" for="14105240_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#14105240"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-21
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="14105240"
    >
Demolition for erection of new structure or new use.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-14105240" data-guid="14105240"></div>
        <div id="questions-14105240" data-guid="14105240" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="14105240_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">When a building is to be demolished to permit the erection of a new structure or for purposes of a new use, such fact shall be stated in the application for such permit. Where a new structure or new use requires approval from the Board of Zoning Appeals in accordance with Chapter <a class="xref" guid="38067105" href="38067105#38067105">375</a> of the Code of the City of Albany, a permit shall not be issued until such Board has granted necessary approvals for the proposed new structure or new use.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681146"
      id="7681146"
      data-guid="7681146"
      data-position="3062"
      data-full-title="§ 133-22: Demolition procedure."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681146_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681146_label" for="7681146_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681146"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-22
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681146"
    >
Demolition procedure.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681146" data-guid="7681146"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681146" data-guid="7681146" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681146_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">When a building is to be demolished, after the trim has been removed the work shall commence at the top story and proceed story by story. No structural portion of any story shall be removed until the story above has been demolished. No structural material shall be placed upon the floor of any such building in the course of demolition.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681147"
      id="7681147"
      data-guid="7681147"
      data-position="3063"
      data-full-title="§ 133-23: Material to be wet down."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681147_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681147_label" for="7681147_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681147"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-23
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681147"
    >
Material to be wet down.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681147" data-guid="7681147"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681147" data-guid="7681147" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681147_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">All mason material shall be properly wet down to lay the dust incident to its removal.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681148"
      id="7681148"
      data-guid="7681148"
      data-position="3064"
      data-full-title="§ 133-24: Notice to owner of adjoining properly."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681148_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681148_label" for="7681148_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681148"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-24
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681148"
    >
Notice to owner of adjoining properly.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681148" data-guid="7681148"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681148" data-guid="7681148" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681148_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The owner or his agent of any structure to be demolished shall give not less than five business days' notice to the owner or owners of adjoining property or their authorized agents.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681149"
      id="7681149"
      data-guid="7681149"
      data-position="3065"
      data-full-title="§ 133-25: Rules and regulations. "
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681149_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681149_label" for="7681149_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681149"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-25
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681149"
    >
Rules and regulations.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681149" data-guid="7681149"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681149" data-guid="7681149" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681149_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Added <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">10-20-1986</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The Commissioner of Buildings is hereby authorized and empowered to promulgate additional rules and regulations not inconsistent with the provisions of this code and which are intended to effectuate the purposes and intent of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681110" href="7681110#7681110">1</a> and/or necessary in the interests of the public welfare, safety or convenience.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
      </div>
  </div>

            </div>
          </div>
        </main>
